# Beorn the Fierce: "At the beginning of combat on your turn, put a trample counter on up to one target creature you control. It
# becomes a Bear in addition to its other types. Then if you control three or more Bears, draw two cards." On turn 1 Beorn targets
# himself (a trample counter, already a Bear): one Bear, nothing drawn. Bot2's Forest Bear, cast on turn 2, is not pumped
# ("Other Bears you control") and, with Grizzly Bears on turn 3, does not make Bot1's Bears three: "up to one" is chosen as none
# and two Bears (one short of three) still draw nothing; Bot2's Bear is a 2/2 throughout.

